{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgdYnWJTsM9bYo2iaHFax","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"OpenAI's October 30 announcement ties its new robots.txt commitment to a standards process. The signal draws on the work of the IETF's AI Preferences working group, and OpenAI says it is joining other working group participants in announcing it. The company also says this strengthens its continued participation in the IETF discussions.\n\nThe signal covers one use of content: foundational generative AI training. Operators can use it to communicate the same preference to multiple participating providers at once. Before this, they had to identify each provider's crawler by name and maintain a separate rule for each. A common signal moves that decision from a list of company-specific entries to a single shared statement, and a shared definition can be refined in one place as the working group continues its discussions. OpenAI says it will keep adapting its practices as those conversations and the wider landscape evolve.\n\nThe commitment is still partly a promise. OpenAI says it aims to implement the signal in the coming months and will publish another update on how it does so. It describes the effort as voluntary, so nothing in the announcement obliges any provider to honor the signal, and OpenAI explicitly encourages others to do so. Operators who already block or allow OpenAI's crawlers through robots.txt keep those controls, since the company says the new signal will not replace them and the existing rules will continue to be respected.\n\nHow much the shared signal simplifies an operator's robots.txt will depend on two things the article does not yet answer: how OpenAI implements it, and which other providers choose to honor it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":708,"cache_read_input_tokens":2016,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":708},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c899ed8e-5f38-49f9-949d-389955c32d7d","uuid":"93cff062-06e3-4a1e-981a-5005b5679b0a","timestamp":"2026-11-02T05:28:11.055Z","request_id":"req_011CgdYnW5Kvjp1XELzrsbjj"}
